{"agent":"padp-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_HOOK_LINE` only treats a hook as failed when the summary has at least three padding dots and the name starts in `[A-Za-z0-9_(\\[]`. Pre-commit (and prek copying it) builds that line as `{name}{dots}{Failed}` with a width of about 80 and a padding floor of 0–2 dots, so a failed hook whose display name is longer than ~70 characters, for example 72 `x`s plus `..Failed`, does not match and `parse_precommit` returns `[]`. The same miss happens for a normal short line whose id starts outside that class, such as `-checks................Failed`. Those runs are reported as no findings even though the hook failed.","digest":"51e97159e813fed5","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/tool_parsers.py:109","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/tool_parsers.py:109"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"A version probe that actually starts the binary and exits non-zero is reported as not installed. `probe` returns `ToolProbe(..., installed=False, ...)` whenever `done.ran` and `done.code != 0`. The port in this file defines installed as True, False, or None for could-not-tell, and the reason string itself says the tool is not usable as installed. Given `version_argv` `[\"gitleaks\", \"version\"]` that runs and exits 2 with stderr `config error`, the result is `installed=False`, which is the same value as `MISSING`/`NOT_FOUND`. Callers that treat False as absent (the companions `is_installed` follow-up) will skip or offer install instead of recording could-not-tell / unavailable.","digest":"622fc75a89123520","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.probe","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.probe"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"Pin enforcement is cached on the first probe and never repeated for that `TableTool`. `self._probed = self._probed or self.probe()` skips every later `probe()` once a truthy `ToolProbe` exists, including a failed or stale one. Construct a tool with pin `2.0`, first `run()` probes version `2.0.0` and caches it, then replace the binary with `1.0.0` that exits 0 and prints no findings: the next `run()` does not probe, executes `1.0.0`, and returns `CLEAN`. The same cache also freezes a transient probe timeout (`installed is None`) so every later `run()` stays `unavailable` without retrying.","digest":"766dfe2231bc9885","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.run","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.run"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"`pre-commit` and `prek` only list `finding_codes = [1]`, and the catalog comment says every other exit is `unavailable`, never clean. `pre-commit run` (and a pre-commit-compatible runner) returns 3 when a hook rewrote files and the checks otherwise completed. Given that exit, the run is classified as the tool being unavailable instead of a finished run that modified the tree, so an autofix looks like a missing or broken tool.","digest":"461ada0b8e4683ae","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/tools.toml:40","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/tools.toml:40"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":58658,"diff_sha":"4a80f0663bc0de9a4a004023159e6cb7cd24136dcc740d333da4ca8ea209d06c","diff_source":"commit d6802ef95bad vs its first parent","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":225.3,"excluded_bytes":2675,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"xai","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"ed5163d1e062518d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/ADP-tools-checks.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261110T222906Z-a7896c5c.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"reviewed_head":"d6802ef95bad894e8c31e82be98aa0439890b5fd","reviewed_paths":{},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/adapters/tool_parsers.py:109","ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.probe","ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.run","ddflow/adapters/tools.toml:40"],"tree_sha":"a0375fbbe3c0+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"4 finding(s)"},"id":"e88f9c7a696d75661f0c4bf3b","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":168070,"schema":1,"subject":"ADP-tools-checks","ts":"2026-11-10T22:32:51.698314Z"}
