{"agent":"padp-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The padding-floor change does not answer the confirmed probe. `_HOOK_LINE` still requires the hook name to start in `[A-Za-z0-9_(\\[]`, so `parse_precommit(\"pre-commit\", \"-checks................Failed\")` still returns `[]`. A real pre-commit summary line whose id starts with `-` (or any other character outside that class) is dropped even when it has many padding dots and ends in `Failed`.","digest":"73d8a8e7e2736e22","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/tool_parsers.py:_HOOK_LINE","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/tool_parsers.py:_HOOK_LINE"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new guard only re-probes when the cached probe is missing or not `usable`. A successful pin check is still stored forever. Construct a tool pinned to `2.0`, let the first `run()` probe `2.0.0` and cache a usable probe, then replace the binary with `1.0.0` that exits 0 and prints no findings: the next `run()` skips `probe()`, executes `1.0.0`, and returns `CLEAN`. The comment claims a binary change is covered; the `if` does not do that.","digest":"eb579e34124df0a0","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.run","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/adapters/tools.py:TableTool.run"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3653,"diff_sha":"2b4ea881ffa079ac6d56a364e831938536d994f0c3aa70d415a1394a1eddf610","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/ADP-tools-checks","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":24.2,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"cf0e8ec88428b4bf","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/ADP-tools-checks.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261110T225203Z-dc5f6931.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"revi